{"story":{"what":"In TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo, a member whose key kind differs from the earlier members is now skipped right after the DoNotMixStringAndIntKeys diagnostic is reported. Members are only added to the intMembers and stringMembers dictionaries when their key is not already there, so a duplicate key no longer causes an exception after KeysMustBeUnique is reported. The same edits are made in both the property loop and the field loop. New analyzer and execution tests cover SuppressSourceGeneration = true types, and the README gains a section on opting out of source generation.","why":"The requirement (MP-2234) says the analyzer stopped reporting diagnostics for [MessagePackObject(SuppressSourceGeneration = true)] types after 3.1.0. In the old code, a type with duplicate keys or mixed key kinds made the collector throw: Dictionary.Add got a duplicate key, or intKey!.Value was read on a null key. The analyzer then failed instead of reporting. After the change it reports the problem and keeps going, so the remaining checks still run for suppressed types.","touches":[{"symbol":"TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo","file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","note":"Skips members with a mismatched key kind and guards dictionary inserts against duplicate int and string keys, in both the property and field loops."},{"symbol":"SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests","file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","note":"New analyzer tests for suppressed types: MsgPack004, 015, 003 and 005, the absence of source-generation-only diagnostics, and one duplicate-key case for a non-suppressed type."},{"symbol":"SuppressedSourceGenerationTests","file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","note":"New execution tests: no generated formatter exists for a suppressed type, and the type round-trips through the standard options."},{"symbol":"README section 'Opting out of source generation'","file":"README.md","note":"Documents which analyzer rules still apply to suppressed types and which do not."}]},"claims":[{"requirementItemId":"N1","text":"In both the property loop and the field loop, after DoNotMixStringAndIntKeys is reported for a member whose key kind differs from the first keyed member, the member is skipped with continue. The code no longer goes on to read intKey!.Value or stringKey for that member.","kind":"behaviour","hunkIds":["h2","h5"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1005,"endLine":1009,"quote":"continue; // The key kind does not match the other members; the diagnostic is reported, so skip this member."},{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1145,"endLine":1149,"quote":"continue; // The key kind does not match the other members; the diagnostic is reported, so skip this member."}]},{"requirementItemId":"N1","text":"For int keys, a member is added to intMembers only if its key is not already present. A duplicate int key now leaves the first member in place and no longer throws from Dictionary.Add after KeysMustBeUnique is reported. This applies to both properties and fields.","kind":"behaviour","hunkIds":["h3","h6"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1023,"endLine":1026,"quote":"if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(member.IntKey))
                        {
                            intMembers.Add(member.IntKey, (member, item.Type));"},{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1163,"endLine":1166,"quote":"if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(member.IntKey))"}]},{"requirementItemId":"N1","text":"For string keys, a member is added to stringMembers only if its key is not already present. A duplicate string key now leaves the first member in place instead of throwing from Dictionary.Add. This applies to both properties and fields.","kind":"behaviour","hunkIds":["h4","h7"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1039,"endLine":1042,"quote":"if (!stringMembers.ContainsKey(member.StringKey))
                        {
                            stringMembers.Add(member.StringKey, (member, item.Type));"},{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1179,"endLine":1182,"quote":"if (!stringMembers.ContainsKey(member.StringKey))"}]},{"requirementItemId":"F1","text":"New analyzer tests check that a SuppressSourceGeneration = true type gets three diagnostics: MsgPack004 for a public member without a Key, MsgPack015 for a keyed private member without AllowPrivate, and MsgPack003 for a member whose type is not a MessagePackObject.","kind":"test","hunkIds":["h9"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":24,"endLine":27,"quote":"public string {|MsgPack004:Member|} { get; set; }"},{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":42,"endLine":46,"quote":"[{|MsgPack015:MessagePackObject(SuppressSourceGeneration = true)|}]"},{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":65,"endLine":69,"quote":"public Other {|MsgPack003:Member|} { get; set; }"}]},{"requirementItemId":"N1","text":"New analyzer tests check that suppressed types with duplicate int keys, duplicate string keys, or mixed int and string keys get MsgPack005 on the second member. The tests expect no other diagnostics, so an analyzer exception would fail them.","kind":"test","hunkIds":["h9"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":81,"endLine":91,"quote":"public async Task DuplicateIntKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure()"},{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":103,"endLine":113,"quote":"public async Task DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure()"},{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":125,"endLine":135,"quote":"{|MsgPack005:[Key(""Member2"")]"}]},{"requirementItemId":"N2","text":"A test checks that a type without SuppressSourceGeneration and with duplicate int keys gets MsgPack005 and nothing else.","kind":"test","hunkIds":["h9"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":147,"endLine":157,"quote":"public async Task DuplicateKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailureForGeneratedTypes()"}]},{"requirementItemId":"F2","text":"A test checks that a suppressed type with AllowPrivate, a private keyed field and an init property with an initializer gets no diagnostics. This means MsgPack011, MsgPack016 and MsgPack017 are not reported for suppressed types.","kind":"test","hunkIds":["h9"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":169,"endLine":180,"quote":"public async Task SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed()"}]},{"requirementItemId":"F1","text":"Two execution tests check a SuppressSourceGeneration = true type. The first checks that GeneratedMessagePackResolver returns no formatter for it. The second checks that the type round-trips with MessagePackSerializerOptions.Standard.","kind":"test","hunkIds":["h8"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":20,"endLine":24,"quote":"Assert.Null(GeneratedMessagePackResolver.Instance.GetFormatter<SuppressedSourceGenerationType>());"},{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":29,"endLine":35,"quote":"byte[] bytes = MessagePackSerializer.Serialize(value, MessagePackSerializerOptions.Standard);"}]},{"requirementItemId":"F1","text":"The README gains a section on SuppressSourceGeneration = true. It lists the analyzer rules that still apply to such types (MsgPack004, 005, 015, 003 and 012) and says that MsgPack011, 016 and 017 are not reported for them.","kind":"docs","hunkIds":["h1"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"README.md","side":"new","startLine":1620,"endLine":1625,"quote":"The analyzer still validates these types, because they are serialized at run time and must still have a valid contract:"},{"file":"README.md","side":"new","startLine":1632,"endLine":1632,"quote":"The analyzer does not report the partial-class requirement ([MsgPack011](doc/analyzers/MsgPack011.md)) or the AOT-only checks ([MsgPack016](doc/analyzers/MsgPack016.md) and [MsgPack017](doc/analyzers/MsgPack017.md)) for these types, because they only apply when a formatter is generated."}]}]}
